md5-simd — third-party notices
==============================

The crate is distributed under Apache-2.0. RFC 1321 supplies the MD5 algorithm,
constants, and standard vectors. The portable Rust and batch implementations
are maintained in this tree.

Vendored scalar compression
---------------------------

src/simd/single_x86.rs and src/simd/single_stream.rs adapt the compression path
from fast-md5 1.0.0, Copyright (c) 2026, Latigo LLC, under BSD-2-Clause.
Source: https://github.com/ogital-net/fast-md5
The assembly's upstream provenance is animetosho/md5-optimisation (PD/CC0):
https://github.com/animetosho/md5-optimisation

The integration retains the assembly body, uses the shared in-tree K constants,
and routes framing and state management through the crate's own implementation.
These files are compiled for x86_64 with opt unless force-portable is enabled.
No third-party streaming or HMAC API is re-exported.

Design references
-----------------

md5-many (https://github.com/Small-Ku/md5-many), MIT OR Apache-2.0, informed the
separation of single-message and batch APIs and differential testing. Its source
is not vendored. RustCrypto md-5 is a development-only correctness reference.

